461
00:38:27,440 --> 00:38:34,140
Suppose you take the
alternating harmonic series,

462
00:38:34,140 --> 00:38:36,230
Remember that this thing here--

463
00:38:36,230 --> 00:38:39,470
that's the harmonic series.

464
00:38:39,470 --> 00:38:41,790
This here is divergent.

465
00:38:45,580 --> 00:38:46,860
I actually proved--

466
00:38:46,860 --> 00:38:51,500
I proved, or at least I outlined
in class, why this series here

467
00:38:51,500 --> 00:38:53,150
is convergent.

468
00:38:53,150 --> 00:38:57,110
And this is-- and it's just--

469
00:38:57,110 --> 00:39:00,300
again, the idea
here is that if you

470
00:39:00,300 --> 00:39:02,700
take-- so you have
something which is called

471
00:39:02,700 --> 00:39:05,460
the alternating series test.

472
00:39:05,460 --> 00:39:06,885
So this is a--

473
00:39:06,885 --> 00:39:08,260
I'm coming back
to your question.

474
00:39:08,260 --> 00:39:10,952
Just a second.

475
00:39:10,952 --> 00:39:13,120
And this is closely
related to that.

476
00:39:13,120 --> 00:39:20,160
So the alternating series test
is that if you take a sequence

477
00:39:20,160 --> 00:39:29,400
a n of non-negative numbers
and a n converges to 0--

478
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:34,440
